# Keeps the Docker build context small and, more importantly, keeps
# secrets and local state OUT of image layers. `.env` is excluded on
# purpose -- env vars reach containers via docker-compose.yml's
# `environment`/`env_file`, never baked into an image at build time.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.vscode
.idea
tests/load/output
docs
README.md

# Terraform: provider binaries are hundreds of MB, and state/tfvars hold
# real secrets (DB password, Redis key) -- neither belongs in a build
# context, even for an intermediate stage.
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/terraform.tfvars
**/*.auto.tfvars
